# 🫁 TB Detection using Deep Learning

## 📌 Overview

This project detects **Tuberculosis (TB)** from chest X-ray images using a **Convolutional Neural Network (CNN)**.
It provides an automated system to assist early diagnosis.

---

## 🚀 Features

* Image preprocessing (grayscale, resize, normalization)
* CNN-based classification (TB vs Normal)
* Evaluation (accuracy, confusion matrix, ROC curve)
* Grad-CAM visualization
* Streamlit web app for prediction

---

## 📂 Dataset (Auto Download)

This project uses the **TB Chest X-ray Dataset** from Kaggle.

👉 The dataset is **automatically downloaded using `kagglehub`** — no manual download needed.

### 🔹 Dataset Code (used in project)

```python id="8n1k0k"
import kagglehub

path = kagglehub.dataset_download(
    "tawsifurrahman/tuberculosis-tb-chest-xray-dataset"
)

print("Dataset path:", path)
```

---

## ⚙️ Installation

### 1. Clone the repository

```bash id="y0v0zj"
git clone https://github.com/vaishnavi123-cOde/tb_detection.git
cd tb_detection
```

---

### 2. Install dependencies

```bash id="b2j9wq"
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

---

### 3. Install KaggleHub (if not installed)

```bash id="3l7v9x"
pip install kagglehub
```

---

## ▶️ Usage

### 🔹 Step 1: Train the model (downloads dataset automatically)

```bash id="7n4p4o"
python train.py
```

✔ This will:

* Download dataset (~600MB)
* Preprocess images
* Train CNN model
* Save model in `models/`

---

### 🔹 Step 2: Evaluate model

```bash id="k2u4yb"
python evaluate.py
```

---

### 🔹 Step 3: Predict using image

```bash id="zv0gzt"
python predict.py
```

---

### 🔹 Step 4: Run Streamlit app

```bash id="0m8qj1"
streamlit run app.py
```

---

## 📊 Results

* Accuracy: ~97%
* AUC Score: ~0.989
* Improved TB detection using:

  * Class weights
  * Threshold tuning

---

## 🧠 Model Details

* CNN (Conv2D, MaxPooling, Dense)
* Input: 128 × 128 grayscale images
* Loss: Binary Crossentropy
* Optimizer: Adam

---

## ⚠️ Important Notes

* Dataset is **not included in repo** (large size)
* It is downloaded automatically using KaggleHub
* Model file (`.keras`) is also excluded

---

## 🖥️ Application

The Streamlit app allows:

* Uploading X-ray images
* Predicting TB or Normal
* Displaying results instantly

